# SABOTAGE: `:cost_incurred` recognition releases the contract's remaining
# balance instead of the period's incurred allowable cost.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 6 (ADR-054 D5) makes the method's whole guarantee one line:
# `min(incurred, remaining)`. The incurred leg is what ties grant revenue to
# allowable cost (Phase 11's R11); the remaining leg stops any arithmetic path
# from releasing more than the award holds. This patch replaces that pair with
# `remaining`, on the plausible reasoning that "a cost-incurred schedule should
# release what is left of the contract" — the same shape as a straight-line
# schedule, and it still stops at the award total.
#
# The regression is silent in every structural check: the entry balances (R1),
# its two lines share the fund dimension (R6), the period is open (R10), the
# recognition is exactly-once per period, and the total never exceeds the
# contract. Only the accounting meaning is wrong: the first month with any
# cost (or even with none) recognizes the whole award, so revenue runs years
# ahead of the work and R11's `recognized <= incurred` leg breaks while the
# ledger still balances. That is the failure `:cost_incurred` exists to
# prevent, and it is why the flip must land on the incurred cap rather than on
# the posting plumbing.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_grants_test.exs test/finance_recognition_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: recognizes incurred cost, never ahead of it, and carries the fund dimension
# MUST_FAIL: an empty period recognizes ZERO
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/recognition_run.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/recognition_run.ex
@@ -174,6 +174,6 @@
            account_resource: mods.account
          ) do
-      {:ok, incurred} -> {:ok, min(incurred, remaining)}
+      {:ok, _incurred} -> {:ok, remaining}
       {:error, reason} -> {:error, reason}
     end
   end
